+# Independent creation probe
+
+Run `python tools/run_independent_creation_probe.py creations/probe-NEW` with a new destination.
+
+Observed on 2026-09-12:
+
+1. A free-form request to invent a browser experience returned `HOLD_NO_SUPPORTED_SYNTHESIS_BLUEPRINT`.
+2. An exact `local-interaction` interface goal plus labels/color produced a tested detached candidate. The machine selected shell, theme and interaction packages and generated a compose -> verify -> report recipe.
+3. This assistant-authored driver explicitly invoked the tested candidate, retained its actual output and checked independent report equality. It did not install the candidate.
+4. Asking for `reactive-light` returned `HOLD_MISSING_ORGAN_INTERFACE`.
+5. Live capability and installed-organ JSON bytes stayed unchanged.
+6. Chrome preview rendered the unmodified page. Clicking Light the lantern changed the button to The lantern is lit. The hosted raw page was byte-for-byte identical to the machine output.
+
+The outcome is deterministic composition from existing source templates. No new HTML/CSS/JavaScript semantics or free-form intent interpretation were invented. The lantern wording was supplied by the assistant: actual output is a button label and body-state change, not a lighting simulation.
+
+The experiment viewer is separately assistant-authored and clearly labels that distinction. Browser observations are outside the driver; its report keeps browser_observed_by_this_driver false.
+
+This repeatable experiment is the improvement: future machine changes can be compared against the same explicit open-ended, supported-composition and missing-interface boundaries. No new authority or automatic-admission path was added.
